  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 334035ecee4cd9f4d8be1f6282ba7c23, type: 3}
  m_Name: VerseOne_DialogueData_2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Messages:
  - Prayers are sealed contracts for mortals to follow. Humans were carved to be
    followers of the divine, forbidden to become gods themselves from borrowed power
    or influence.
  - Divine authority always look for something in return even if it's their nature
    to aid humanity. History has proven those who only take are granted punishment
    for eternity.
  - What promise sealed the first verse of the Ancient Prayer?
  ButtonOneText: We ask that thou never abandon us, for without thee we are nothing.
  ButtonTwoText: 'We pledge our faithfulness through structures to allow your light
    to illuminate your beauty across the land. '
  ButtonThreeText: We pledge our faithfulness through sculptures of Her Grace's image
    every dusk and every dawn, now and forevermore.
  correctButtonNumber: 3
